{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/189713-extended-family-for-the-littlest-gameline-crossline-book-recommendations","id":189713,"title":"Extended Family for the Littlest Gameline - Crossline Book Recommendations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-06T17:28:16-07:00","id":189713,"title":"Extended Family for the Littlest Gameline - Crossline Book Recommendations","content":"As I may have mentioned elsewhere, I'm in the process of reading through as much of the nWoD as I can; I finished the current corpus of published Geist books about a month or two back, opted to read some of the bluebook material before I moved on to Promethean - chiefly Antagonists and Second Sight - and found a decent amount of useful material beyond that specifically pointed out in the Geist corebook, i.e. the zombie rules and the psychic powers.<br /> <br /> For starters, both Second Sight and Antagonists contain information on cults, though with different focuses - the Entropic Things and Demons of the Outer Darkness from Second Sight's Cults of Things That Must Not Be both seem particularly fitting for chthonians and other strange things out of the Underworld, while Antagonists' more detailed look at the types and structures of cult give a general idea of how the more hardline krewes (or the mortal hangers-on thereof) might operate.<br /> <br /> Then there's tidbits like Antagonists' fourth chapter containing what seems a good example of weird things one might find in the Underworld - toxicum mold is worrying stuff - or Second Sight's emphasis on how psychic powers tend to impact their possessors' psyche in the having of them - the opening fiction and sample story in particular do a good job of highlighting the effects of being host to a power not entirely under your control.<br /> <br /> So now I'm reading Immortals, whose utility in constructing abmortals should be fairly obvious; the mechanics for how societies of body thieves work seem to call back to Second Sight's mechanics for thaumaturgy paths, and of course blood bathers are practically archetypical in terms of &quot;immortal who stays immortal by maintaining a body count,&quot; though Pig provides a good example of how that can get more complicated and Shawn's frankly worrying genesis hooks in well enough to the matter of things that make Reapers ask serious questions.<br /> <br /> All that said, does anybody have any other bits of recommended reading for Geist that isn't part of the gameline proper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:07:58-07:00","id":189727,"title":"","content":"Well, off the top of my hat, I remember Mage the Awakening; Summoners having a section about things highly resonant with Death that an Awakened summoner might call up. They mention Cthonians for one, and other than that, provides a handful of fairly interesting creatures which one can make strange dealings with. One in particular i liked, which were something like a raven in a tree which you had to climb with entirely mortal means, otherwise it rejected the &quot;deal&quot; you were making (unknowingly, though you might be). Its a fair bit of time since I looked it over, but I remember finding it fairly interesting in relation to Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:30:24-07:00","id":189754,"title":"","content":"<i>Dancers in the Dusk</i> has some info on what the dying dream about, along with a Morphean called the Pale Brother who might be an incarnation of Death.<br /> <br /> One of the pieces of microfiction in <i>Chicago</i> could be interpreted as a dying man meeting a geist. The one with the narrator screaming &quot;I'm not dead!&quot; as the thing approaches him.<br /> <br /> <i>Mummy: The Curse</i> has a bunch of new ghost Numina. Some Utterances that affect ghosts could also provide some bits of cosmological necromystery for Sin-Eaters to puzzle over, like the one that sucks ghosts into a lake of fire until the Arisen vomits them up again to do its bidding.<br /> <br /> The Moros chapter in <i>Tome of the Watchtowers</i> has some cool stuff on various philosophies of death, like whether or not Hiroshima cheapened the concept.<br /> <br /> There is, of course, <i>Ghost Stories</i>, but that basically goes without saying.<br /> <br /> I recall the corebook for Geist mentioning <i>Midnight Roads</i>. Might be worth a look.<br /> <br /> Finally, the only other thing that comes to me right now is the chapter on Sin-Eaters in <i>Mortal Remains</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:37:17-07:00","id":189893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/189713-extended-family-for-the-littlest-gameline-crossline-book-recommendations?p=189754#post189754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Mummy: The Curse</i> has a bunch of new ghost Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of order: A sizeable chunk of those are nearly direct ports from the first chapter of Antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T23:08:50-07:00","id":189945,"title":"","content":"My <b>Geist</b> game has made heavy use of <i>Second Sight </i>and <i>Antagonists.</i> I will second <i>Summoners</i> as being very good...I definitely have gotten some good use out of it. The Cthonians are useful, the Numbers Station stuff works for Geist, and the Men in Black work for dealing with a Krewe that wants to solve every issue by overpowering it. Some ghost stuff there is good too.<br /> <br /> <i>WoD: Immortals</i> I have also gotten a fair amount of use of. Also, <i>WoD: Slashers</i> does not make for even powered antagonists but also make for antagonists Sin-Eaters might fight. I would say that with the above three mentioned earlier in thread are my big five recommendations.<br /> <br /> Honerable mention to <i>Glimpses of the Unknown</i>, which has a short Sin-Eater section with a Ceremony.<br /> <br /> Secondarily, as noted above<i> Midnight Roads</i> and <i>Ghost Stories</i> are useful. <i>Ghost Stories</i> is hard to use out of the box due to Sin-Eater powers but has some use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T00:13:42-07:00","id":189989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/189713-extended-family-for-the-littlest-gameline-crossline-book-recommendations?p=189893#post189893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order: A sizeable chunk of those are nearly direct ports from the first chapter of Antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. But even there, they\u2019re revised and expanded. And perhaps <i>the single</i> most important of them <i>isn\u2019t</i> a port: Lucid Dead gives you playable ghosts. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T06:05:29-07:00","id":190198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/189713-extended-family-for-the-littlest-gameline-crossline-book-recommendations?p=189893#post189893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order: A sizeable chunk of those are nearly direct ports from the first chapter of Antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. I have not read <i>Antagonists</i>. Pardon.<br /> <br /> Some Vampire books also might have relevant/interesting points in them. Like the...Dragolescu bloodline, I believe, in <i>Ordo Dracul</i>, I also believe. The one that gets the Essentiaphagia Discipline. Also, <i>The Beast that Haunts the Blood</i> mentions that ghosts tend to hang around Nosferatu for whatever reason, and includes some relevant merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T13:14:16-07:00","id":198143,"title":"","content":"The Mystikoi from <i>Ancient Bloodlines</i> are a small bloodline of vampires originally from Armenia who practice a sort of twisted form of Gnostic Christianity significantly influenced by Manichaeism. They regard the Beast as a sort of spiritual guide, and have a unique discipline that allows them to perceive and communicate with entities in twilight while riding the wave of frenzy.<br /> <br /> The Sta-Au, from the same book, are a strange North American bloodline originally associated with the Ktunaxa and Blackfoot tribes who are unusual in that they can &quot;adopt&quot; new members from any of the clans. Like the Dragolescu and the Mystikoi they have unique abilities that allow them to see and communicate with ghosts, but they can actually go one step further and temporarily &quot;fade away&quot; into twilight, becoming ghosts themselves for most mechanical purposes.<br /> <br /> These days the Sta-Au have spread out from their place of origin, making their territory in barren places that they call the &quot;Land of the Worms&quot;, which is made up of isolated pockets of land that seem to attract ghosts and are inimical to all living things besides vermin and parasites. Areas that are part of the Land of the Worms have a number of unusual properties, not the least of which is that any human that dies there invariably becomes a ghost, with the area itself acting as their anchor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-15-2014, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}